# LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows and run on Linux: the working copy is
# rsynced to WSL or to a cluster, so a CRLF checkout is copied verbatim to a
# filesystem that cannot use it. Shell scripts fail outright, with
# "$'\r': command not found" and then "set: pipefail: invalid option name",
# and `bash -n` does not catch it because `set -euo pipefail\r` is only invalid
# when it runs.
#
# Git already stores LF; the conversion happens on checkout under
# core.autocrlf=true, which is the Windows default. These rules override it for
# anyone who clones, so nobody has to know to set core.autocrlf themselves.
#
# text=auto lets Git detect text and leave binaries alone; eol=lf pins the
# checkout. The explicit binary lines below are belt and braces for the formats
# actually in this repository, so a heuristic never has the chance to mangle
# the Word guide or an image.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.docx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gz   binary
*.rds  binary
*.img  binary
*.tar  binary
